# Native UI — shell vs content (CORE METHOD)

This is the **absolute, unskippable requirement** for Saaf Milk native UI.
Authority: `PHASE14_8_15A_SHELL_VS_CONTENT.md`. Proven by the Owner Work six-entry correction.

## Hard rule

Any entry surface used by **two or more roles** MUST separate:

1. **Role-neutral content** — form, loading, failure, draft leave-guard presentation. No `OwnerSection` / `CashierSection` / `OperationsSection`. No foreign bottom nav.
2. **Role-owned shell** — that role’s scaffold, nav, snackbar host, Back/exit path.
3. **Foundation proof** — host-role chrome present, foreign chrome absent, Back returns to the host home, session stays authenticated.

Mounting another role’s full screen (Cashier Collect, Ops Deliveries, etc.) inside Owner — or translating foreign nav events — is a **P0 defect**, not a shortcut.

## Do

- Split content first; wrap with each role’s shell (`OwnerXxxEntryScreen`, Cashier/Ops public screen).
- Feature package depends **outward** only (owner → collection/operations/sale). Shared content never imports a role package.
- Dirty drafts: `EntryLeaveGuard` on hardware Back **and** bottom-nav exits.
- Inventory `COVERED` rows must name real Foundation/workflow tests — never `workflow_test=-` for a hosted entry.
- Before claiming done: run the host role `qaScreen` gate that includes those Foundation tests.

## Do not

- Ship “connected” because a Work tile callback opens a foreign screen.
- Treat launcher/callback-only tests as hosted-entry coverage.
- Skip shell split “temporarily” to move to the next screen (Records, More, etc.).
- Flatten roles: Owner / Cashier / Ops homes stay distinct; only **content** is shared.

## Done check (every multi-role entry)

- [ ] Content has no role nav / section enums
- [ ] Each host role has its own wrapper + Back path
- [ ] Foundation: host chrome ✓, foreign chrome ✗, Back → host home, session intact
- [ ] Inventory points at those tests
- [ ] Host `qaScreen` PASS
